From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Dangoor <omerdn1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:33:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ios): bind the XCTest runner to a token

The runner's HTTP server answered anyone who could reach its loopback
port, so a Maestro process pointed at the wrong port could drive a
simulator it didn't start, and when its liveness probe found that port
busy it treated the runner as its own and could stop or replace it.

The runner now answers only requests that carry the token it was
started with, in the X-Maestro-Runner-Token header. Maestro passes the
token next to PORT: TEST_RUNNER_MAESTRO_RUNNER_TOKEN for xcodebuild and
SIMCTL_CHILD_MAESTRO_RUNNER_TOKEN for simctl and devicectl launches.
Every other request gets HTTP 401 with a JSON body naming the reason
(missing header, wrong token, or a runner started without a token),
and does nothing. That includes /status and unknown paths. The
comparison runs in constant time, in MaestroDriverLib's RunnerToken.

If MAESTRO_RUNNER_TOKEN is set, every runner the process starts uses
it. Otherwise each launch gets a random 256-bit token from
SecureRandom. XCTestDriverClient adds the header to every request
through an OkHttp interceptor, and the installer's status probe sends
it too.

The installer now tells three states apart: its own runner (2xx), a
runner that holds the port but refuses the token (401), and no runner.
On a 401 it doesn't launch, kill or uninstall anything. start() fails
with IOSDriverPortTakenException, and uninstall() leaves that runner
alone. The command log masks the token, and withInjectedShellEnvVars
leaves MAESTRO_RUNNER_TOKEN out, so flows and maestro cloud uploads never
see it.
